  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "mustn't: prohibition",
      "title_form": "Mustn't: prohibición",
      "title_target": "Mustn't: prohibition",
      "description_md_form": "**Mustn't** se usa para decir que algo **no está permitido** o que es una **regla**. Es la forma negativa de *must* y significa **no debes** o **no puedes**.\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n> **Subject + mustn't + verbo base**\n\n**Ejemplos:**\n\n- *You **mustn't smoke** here.* = No debes fumar aquí.\n- *We **mustn't eat** in the hospital.* = No debemos comer en el hospital.\n\n**Importante:** *Mustn't* es una **prohibición fuerte**. No es un consejo, es una regla. Si quieres dar un consejo, usa *shouldn't* (no deberías).\n\n**Tabla rápida:**\n\n| Pronombre | Afirmativo | Negativo |\n|-----------|------------|----------|\n| I | must | mustn't |\n| You | must | mustn't |\n| He/She/It | must | mustn't |\n| We | must | mustn't |\n| They | must | mustn't |\n\n**Recuerda:** *Mustn't* no cambia con la persona. Siempre es *mustn't* + verbo base.",
      "description_md_target": "**Mustn't** is used to say that something is **not allowed** or that it is a **rule**. It is the negative form of *must* and means **no debes** or **no puedes**.\n\n**Structure:**\n\n> **Subject + mustn't + base verb**\n\n**Examples:**\n\n- *You **mustn't smoke** here.* = No debes fumar aquí.\n- *We **mustn't eat** in the hospital.* = No debemos comer en el hospital.\n\n**Important:** *Mustn't* is a **strong prohibition**. It is not advice, it is a rule. If you want to give advice, use *shouldn't*.\n\n**Quick table:**\n\n| Pronoun | Affirmative | Negative |\n|---------|-------------|----------|\n| I | must | mustn't |\n| You | must | mustn't |\n| He/She/It | must | mustn't |\n| We | must | mustn't |\n| They | must | mustn't |\n\n**Remember:** *Mustn't* does not change with the person. It is always *mustn't* + base verb.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + mustn't + base verb",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "mustn't_prohibition",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
